  "frameRatePolicy": "Existing frame-rate settings retained; no new cap or reduction.",
  "implementation": [
    "Retain the one ready native player rig/materials/weapons across painted-world travel. Recreate area-local cast, controllers, collision and environment. Rebind player ownership, position, pose and equipment state; release on chapter disposal.",
    "Overlap independent map, portal, character, material, weapon and melee-clip loading through existing Cocos APIs.",
    "Warm only the current hero/equipment assets already required at startup. Skip verified imported texture aliases in TapTap releases to preserve existing native texture reuse.",
    "Read resident resources using typed Bundle.get and preserve asynchronous callbacks. Fall back to normal load for missing/invalid assets; no extra persistent resource cache.",
    "Omit normal sampling/tangent generation only for painted unlit terrain, retaining its position/index/UV/color data and original continuous collision mesh.",
    "Replace the fixed 120ms ready-screen delay with the first completed render frame.",
    "Prevent per-frame player updates before assembly finishes, and invalidate equipment-display state during transfer so weapons/scabbards are correctly visible."
  ],
  "scope": "No map-size, collision, gameplay, picture-quality, FPS, platform/login, save or package-version changes. No all-map preloading/streaming cache introduced. The persistent player retains equipment variants already prepared during play, as the existing per-area actor did until travel.",
  "method": {
    "engine": "Cocos Creator 3.8.8",
    "runtime": "Windows desktop Chrome, Creator preview 7456; painted world/native hero mode; 844x390 CSS viewport, DPR 3, touch emulation.",
    "startup": "New isolated browser context for each startup, two contexts in one Chrome process per run. Timing is navigation through ready-state plus snapshot collection; server/OS/engine/shader caches were not forcibly purged. These are local startup samples, not cold-install or network-download guarantees.",
    "mapTransition": "Session enter plus full rebuild, ending after one rendered frame in final code. Seven sequential transitions, including first visits and revisits. Same seed and route.",
    "baseline": "temp/loading-v1/baseline.json for maps; verified-baseline.json for startup (same cold-stage instrumentation as final). Earlier and intermediate runs retained in evidence for variability.",
    "limitations": "No iPhone/TapTap measurements. Small local sample; timings vary with caches, JIT, graphics driver and CPU load. Do not promise these percentages on phones."
  },
